# Benchmark logs

BENCHMARKS.md is the short summary. This folder keeps the six logs that best show how Marin was built and checked. Each
log states its gates first, then the results and the decision. Nothing in the source, the tests or CI reads these files.

## Published here

| Log | Milestone | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| [06-server-scheduling](06-server-scheduling.log) | several requests at once | GO |
| [10-shared-prefix](10-shared-prefix.log) | batched prefill (dropped) and a shared system prompt (kept) | NO-GO and GO |
| [22-session-continuity](22-session-continuity.log) | hot and cold sessions on the server | GO |
| [25-qwen35-int8-prefill](25-qwen35-int8-prefill.log) | CUDA INT8 prefill, 2.5x | GO |
| [30-cpu-history-reuse-planner](30-cpu-history-reuse-planner.log) | CPU history reuse, 1,547 s to 468 s | GO |
| [34-v01-final-pass](34-v01-final-pass.log) | v0.1.0 checks, coding audit, server_cold root causes | SHIP |

## Kept only on the author's machine (bench-results/archive)

Logs 01 to 05, 07 to 09, 11 to 21, 23 and 24, 26 to 29 and 31 to 33. They cover the first GPU and CPU work, the
Granite pilot, server sessions and checkpoints, batched decode and memory, the coding mode, the unified terminal,
durable sessions, speculation, model evaluation, hibernation, baselines, CPU decode limits, the performance profile, low-VRAM
recovery, the assistant, code-mode recovery, and the rejected CPU 4-bit, CPU lookup speculation and answer-guard ideas.
Their conclusions are in the tables in BENCHMARKS.md. Logs 01 to 04 are the original 5,752-line BENCHMARKS.md; joined in
file-name order their SHA-256 is `6cf53334a6d2e46d66d60f4203607023e35320cc274ad9a456b58a23fb8f90d0`.
